1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
This announcement is based on current progress.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:06,000
No one knows how things will change in the future.

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Seriously? A trainee?

4
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:12,000
This is absolutely incorrect.

5
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,000
I can't believe that a trainee may 9th place.

6
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,000
I'm just as shocked as you are.

7
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:19,000
Chiri, just be happy.

8
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:22,000
Trainees hardly ever rank in the preliminary report.

9
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Let's both give it everything we have.

10
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Let's give it everything we have.

11
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Is that the confidence of a winner?

12
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Second.

13
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:34,000
I think she's losing it.

14
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Second place is amazing,

15
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:38,000
but she's not happy about it at all.

16
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:39,000
Huh?

17
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:41,000
You're gonna be a successor.

18
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Huh?

19
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:44,000
I saw your poster, Chan-Chi.

20
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:46,000
I saw your poster, Chan-Chi.

21
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:48,000
I saw your poster, Chan-Chi.

22
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:51,000
I saw your poster, Chan-Chi.

23
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:54,000
I saw your poster, Chan-Chi.

24
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:58,000
I just don't understand why you're so gloomy.

25
00:00:58,000 --> 00:00:59,000
I'm not gloomy?

26
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:01,000
Then turn that frown upside down.

27
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:04,000
If you did, you'd be shining like a star by now.

28
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:05,000
That's it.

29
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:07,000
Let's see some sparkle.

30
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Work the camera.

31
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Make it your enduring fan.

32
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:12,000
It should be in love with you from the first snap.

33
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:19,000
Ouch!

34
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:21,000
My bad.

35
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:23,000
My bad.

36
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:24,000
We're up.

37
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:25,000
It should be in love with you,

38
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:28,000
Cheers everyone!

39
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:42,000
Dog회 time.

40
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:48,900
自分の道進むための力にする

41
00:01:48,900 --> 00:01:55,320
心折れそうな長い桜の前

42
00:01:55,320 --> 00:02:02,480
未来があるなら背を向けられない

43
00:02:02,480 --> 00:02:06,320
友よ覚えているかい?

44
00:02:06,320 --> 00:02:10,020
あの日違いあったこの場所

45
00:02:10,020 --> 00:02:14,920
季節の花が咲く

46
00:02:14,920 --> 00:02:19,000
主なきその声聞こえるよ

47
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:23,500
太陽がほら少しずつあたりの

48
00:02:23,500 --> 00:02:28,640
その闇を剥がしてくれるだろ

49
00:02:28,640 --> 00:02:33,080
主なきさあこの時に僕たちは

50
00:02:33,080 --> 00:02:35,820
そう歩き出そう

51
00:02:35,820 --> 00:02:41,720
誰もみんな弱い生き物さ

52
00:02:41,720 --> 00:02:44,800
愛の気配探しながら

53
00:02:44,800 --> 00:02:47,800
先へ進む

54
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:57,380
次回予告

55
00:02:57,380 --> 00:03:02,380
A handshake event just before the General Elections.

56
00:03:02,380 --> 00:03:04,380
Even our guests are excited.

57
00:03:04,380 --> 00:03:06,380
Don't let them be more excited than you.

58
00:03:06,380 --> 00:03:07,380
Right!

59
00:03:07,380 --> 00:03:08,380
Huh?

60
00:03:08,380 --> 00:03:11,380
I'm starting to feel nervous.

61
00:03:11,380 --> 00:03:14,380
They say the handshake event before the General Elections

62
00:03:14,380 --> 00:03:16,380
has an effect on the votes.

63
00:03:16,380 --> 00:03:18,380
Be sure to keep smiling out there.

64
00:03:18,380 --> 00:03:20,380
I can't smile when I'm nervous!

65
00:03:20,380 --> 00:03:21,380
Okay, okay!

66
00:03:21,380 --> 00:03:23,380
Take a deep breath and relax.

67
00:03:23,380 --> 00:03:25,380
Remember, it's a festival.

68
00:03:25,380 --> 00:03:27,380
You've got to enjoy yourselves.

69
00:03:27,380 --> 00:03:29,380
Worrying would just spoil it.

70
00:03:29,380 --> 00:03:30,380
Koji Haru-san?

71
00:03:30,380 --> 00:03:32,380
She has a point.

72
00:03:32,380 --> 00:03:34,380
I voted for you, so you better win.

73
00:03:34,380 --> 00:03:35,380
What?

74
00:03:35,380 --> 00:03:38,380
You know that members aren't allowed to vote for each other.

75
00:03:38,380 --> 00:03:39,380
Oh.

76
00:03:39,380 --> 00:03:41,380
But thanks for the confidence, Megu.

77
00:03:41,380 --> 00:03:42,380
I'll do my best.

78
00:03:42,380 --> 00:03:43,380
Better win.

79
00:03:51,380 --> 00:03:52,380
Chiri?

80
00:03:52,380 --> 00:03:53,380
Girls?

81
00:03:53,380 --> 00:03:55,380
There's something I forgot to tell you.

82
00:03:55,380 --> 00:03:58,380
This time, all of you are going to have lanes of your own.

83
00:03:58,380 --> 00:03:59,380
Individual lanes?

84
00:03:59,380 --> 00:04:01,380
Are you sure about that?

85
00:04:01,380 --> 00:04:04,380
We barely pulled in anyone, even when we had the entire group.

86
00:04:04,380 --> 00:04:06,380
I think you'll be fine.

87
00:04:07,380 --> 00:04:08,380
So many people!

88
00:04:08,380 --> 00:04:10,380
This is your line, Makoto.

89
00:04:10,380 --> 00:04:11,380
And this is Nagi-san.

90
00:04:11,380 --> 00:04:14,380
All these people just for me?

91
00:04:14,380 --> 00:04:17,380
It's the results of the AKB Reformation Campaign.

92
00:04:17,380 --> 00:04:21,380
That and the trainee concert have boosted your popularity.

93
00:04:21,380 --> 00:04:23,380
Look at that line!

94
00:04:23,380 --> 00:04:24,380
It's crazy!

95
00:04:24,380 --> 00:04:26,380
Chiri, that's your line.

96
00:04:26,380 --> 00:04:27,380
Amazing!

97
00:04:27,380 --> 00:04:30,380
That's a successor-level line, Chiri!

98
00:04:30,380 --> 00:04:32,380
What is this?

99
00:04:32,380 --> 00:04:35,380
I felt a pain right in my chest.

100
00:04:38,380 --> 00:04:39,380
Nagisa-chan!

101
00:04:39,380 --> 00:04:40,380
It's me!

102
00:04:40,380 --> 00:04:41,380
Do you remember me?

103
00:04:41,380 --> 00:04:42,380
Oh!

104
00:04:42,380 --> 00:04:43,380
Well, I…

105
00:04:43,380 --> 00:04:44,380
I'm so sorry!

106
00:04:44,380 --> 00:04:47,380
Did we meet at the last handshake event?

107
00:04:47,380 --> 00:04:48,380
Yeah!

108
00:04:48,380 --> 00:04:49,380
I'm just kidding.

109
00:04:49,380 --> 00:04:50,380
Today's my first time.

110
00:04:50,380 --> 00:04:51,380
Huh?

111
00:04:51,380 --> 00:04:54,380
I'm a really big fan, and I've decided to support you.

112
00:04:54,380 --> 00:04:55,380
I'll make sure you're elected!

113
00:04:55,380 --> 00:04:56,380
I promise!

114
00:04:56,380 --> 00:04:57,380
I won't let you down!

115
00:04:57,380 --> 00:04:58,380
Oh!

116
00:04:58,380 --> 00:04:59,380
Thanks!

117
00:04:59,380 --> 00:05:00,380
Alright, keep moving.

118
00:05:00,380 --> 00:05:01,380
See you later, Nagisa!

119
00:05:01,380 --> 00:05:03,380
Make sure you remember me next time!

120
00:05:03,380 --> 00:05:04,380
Oh, wow!

121
00:05:04,380 --> 00:05:05,380
You really are cute, Nagisa!

122
00:05:05,380 --> 00:05:06,380
Nice to meet you!

123
00:05:06,380 --> 00:05:07,380
Thank you!

124
00:05:07,380 --> 00:05:08,380
That's very kind to say!

125
00:05:08,380 --> 00:05:10,380
I'll do my best for the general election, too.

126
00:05:10,380 --> 00:05:12,380
Do your best?

127
00:05:12,380 --> 00:05:13,380
Okay, keep moving!

128
00:05:13,380 --> 00:05:14,380
Keep moving!

129
00:05:14,380 --> 00:05:15,380
Hold on!

130
00:05:15,380 --> 00:05:18,380
The reason you're so determined to work hard for someone like me?

131
00:05:18,380 --> 00:05:19,380
What?

132
00:05:20,380 --> 00:05:23,380
Because you're working so hard, silly!

133
00:05:25,380 --> 00:05:28,380
Your defiance at the AKB trial gave me goosebumps!

134
00:05:28,380 --> 00:05:31,380
That's very kind of you to say. I was just being honest.

135
00:05:31,380 --> 00:05:34,380
I'm convinced that you're the only one who can be AKB's new pioneer!

136
00:05:34,380 --> 00:05:35,380
I couldn't.

137
00:05:35,380 --> 00:05:39,380
The iGirl Noodles commercial that was released last night was great, too!

138
00:05:39,380 --> 00:05:40,380
Keep up the good work!

139
00:05:40,380 --> 00:05:41,380
iGirl Noodles?

140
00:05:41,380 --> 00:05:42,380
I didn't…

141
00:05:43,380 --> 00:05:45,380
Thank you very much!

142
00:05:45,380 --> 00:05:46,380
Chiari!

143
00:05:46,380 --> 00:05:47,380
What's wrong?

144
00:05:47,380 --> 00:05:48,380
Chiari?

145
00:05:49,380 --> 00:05:51,380
Man, I still get butterflies at these things.

146
00:05:51,380 --> 00:05:56,380
Yeah, but out of all the other jobs we do, I think I love these handshake events the most.

147
00:05:56,380 --> 00:05:58,380
Wow, that's surprising.

148
00:05:58,380 --> 00:06:01,380
Last time we did a one of these, you were so scared you couldn't stop crying.

149
00:06:01,380 --> 00:06:03,380
You're so mean sometimes, you know that?

150
00:06:03,380 --> 00:06:04,380
Rivet, rivet!

151
00:06:04,380 --> 00:06:05,380
S-Sonata!

152
00:06:05,380 --> 00:06:06,380
What are you doing?

153
00:06:06,380 --> 00:06:09,380
I have to practice squeezing hands inside the costume!

154
00:06:09,380 --> 00:06:11,380
Try squeezing your ribs, that's a good spot!

155
00:06:12,380 --> 00:06:13,380
Chiari?

156
00:06:15,380 --> 00:06:17,380
Is it already time for us to switch lanes?

157
00:06:17,380 --> 00:06:18,380
Why do people become stronger?

158
00:06:18,380 --> 00:06:27,380
Because if we cry, shout, or fall, we have things we can believe in.

159
00:06:27,380 --> 00:06:32,380
Therefore, I will be a model of success for all of those to come.

160
00:06:32,380 --> 00:06:36,380
And there's a flavor you can believe in, iGirl Noodles.

161
00:06:36,380 --> 00:06:39,380
That is so cool!

162
00:06:39,380 --> 00:06:40,380
No fair!

163
00:06:40,380 --> 00:06:42,380
When did you film a commercial?

164
00:06:42,380 --> 00:06:44,380
I want to do one too!

165
00:06:44,380 --> 00:06:45,380
I didn't.

166
00:06:45,380 --> 00:06:46,380
Huh?

167
00:06:46,380 --> 00:06:48,380
I thought something looked off.

168
00:06:48,380 --> 00:06:50,380
That person in the last shot.

169
00:06:50,380 --> 00:06:52,380
It was an actor made to look like Chiari.

170
00:06:52,380 --> 00:06:56,380
I haven't heard anything about a commercial from iGirl Foods being approved.

171
00:06:56,380 --> 00:06:57,380
Tsubasa-san!

172
00:06:57,380 --> 00:07:01,380
They used the video broadcast from the trial without our permission.

173
00:07:01,380 --> 00:07:03,380
Is that even legal?

174
00:07:03,380 --> 00:07:04,380
It better not be.

175
00:07:04,380 --> 00:07:07,380
We go against laws established by the DGTO regularly.

176
00:07:07,380 --> 00:07:12,380
Even if they use our images without permission, we can't file a lawsuit.

177
00:07:13,380 --> 00:07:15,380
Chiari, go back to your lane, please.

178
00:07:15,380 --> 00:07:16,380
Tsubasa!

179
00:07:16,380 --> 00:07:20,380
The fans here to see you don't know about the story behind that commercial.

180
00:07:26,380 --> 00:07:27,380
Chiari…

181
00:07:27,380 --> 00:07:30,380
I don't get what she was so mad about.

182
00:07:30,380 --> 00:07:33,380
I'd be happy if I were in a commercial!

183
00:07:37,380 --> 00:07:40,380
Did Chiari already go to sleep?

184
00:07:41,380 --> 00:07:43,380
She must be tired.

185
00:07:43,380 --> 00:07:46,380
She shook hands with twice as many people as we did.

186
00:07:48,380 --> 00:07:51,380
On that note, I think I'll turn in as well.

187
00:07:51,380 --> 00:07:52,380
Night.

188
00:07:52,380 --> 00:08:06,380
Are the general elections really so important?

189
00:08:07,380 --> 00:08:09,380
Sayaka-san?

190
00:08:09,380 --> 00:08:10,380
What's she doing up?

191
00:08:13,380 --> 00:08:14,380
And Yuko-san…

192
00:08:14,380 --> 00:08:15,380
Yuko-san!

193
00:08:25,380 --> 00:08:26,380
Good work!

194
00:08:28,380 --> 00:08:29,380
Takamina!

195
00:08:29,380 --> 00:08:33,380
Nice night, huh? Tomo-chin and Yuko-in are practicing over there.

196
00:08:33,380 --> 00:08:34,380
It's insomnia all around.

197
00:08:34,380 --> 00:08:36,380
Well, yeah, we're all excited!

198
00:08:36,380 --> 00:08:38,380
It's the general elections!

199
00:08:44,380 --> 00:09:00,380
Ah-chan, why don't you comfort her?

200
00:09:00,380 --> 00:09:05,380
Honestly, I have a feeling it wouldn't make Hikari happy.

201
00:09:05,380 --> 00:09:11,380
That's right, because it wouldn't! After all, we're both rivals!

202
00:09:11,380 --> 00:09:14,380
Mm-hmm. You're absolutely right!

203
00:09:14,380 --> 00:09:17,380
I hope we can compete against each other in the general elections.

204
00:09:18,380 --> 00:09:20,380
Huh? You bet!

205
00:09:23,380 --> 00:09:25,380
Ah-chan, you liar.

206
00:09:25,380 --> 00:09:26,380
Yuko?

207
00:09:26,380 --> 00:09:29,380
I refuse to end up in second place.

208
00:09:29,380 --> 00:09:32,380
I'll surpass the 13th generation Maeda Atsuko.

209
00:09:32,380 --> 00:09:37,380
I can't let you do that. I'm going to remain first place.

210
00:09:37,380 --> 00:09:38,380
Takamina?

211
00:09:38,380 --> 00:09:41,380
If I don't, Kaneda will lose her example.

212
00:09:41,380 --> 00:09:44,380
I'm going to continue to be the person she looks up to.

213
00:09:44,380 --> 00:09:47,380
Considering she's the girl who could take my place someday.

214
00:09:47,380 --> 00:09:50,380
It's kind of my responsibility, you know?

215
00:09:50,380 --> 00:09:54,380
But no matter who wins, there won't be any hard feelings. Sound good?

216
00:09:54,380 --> 00:09:57,380
But I'll be the one who wins!

217
00:09:57,380 --> 00:10:15,380
Ah-chan, it was a distant star back then. But now, I'll grab it.

218
00:10:15,380 --> 00:10:30,380
Sensei, everyone is fighting their own internal struggle the closer and closer the general elections come.

219
00:10:30,380 --> 00:10:49,380
The center-nova phenomenon that happened to the trainees at the Lancaster concert, using the general elections as a foothold, making the girls compete for the position and pushing them to the level of previous Ah-chan, may be the only way to solve the mystery of the center-nova disappearance and save the girls from a similar fate.

220
00:10:49,380 --> 00:10:59,380
However, is this really the right thing to do?

221
00:10:59,380 --> 00:11:06,380
Sayaka-san and Yuko-san are both working hard for the general elections. I wonder why.

222
00:11:06,380 --> 00:11:10,380
They're going to be ranked for sure. Why worry about it?

223
00:11:12,380 --> 00:11:15,380
Oh! Nagisa!

224
00:11:16,380 --> 00:11:17,380
Mimori-san!

225
00:11:18,380 --> 00:11:22,380
Kanata falls asleep in three seconds once she gets into bed.

226
00:11:23,380 --> 00:11:25,380
I didn't want to disturb her while I worked on all this.

227
00:11:26,380 --> 00:11:28,380
Are you answering letters from fans?

228
00:11:28,380 --> 00:11:29,380
Yep.

229
00:11:29,380 --> 00:11:32,380
That's amazing! You write them all by hand?

230
00:11:32,380 --> 00:11:33,380
That's right.

231
00:11:33,380 --> 00:11:35,380
Can I take a look?

232
00:11:36,380 --> 00:11:37,380
Go ahead.

233
00:11:38,380 --> 00:11:43,380
I can't believe you remember so many details. Even down to the clothes they wore to the handshake event.

234
00:11:44,380 --> 00:11:46,380
Mimori-san, you're an incredibly hard worker.

235
00:11:47,380 --> 00:11:55,380
Thank you. But hard work has nothing to do with remembering things about people I meet. It's so much simpler than that. Truth is, I treasure them.

236
00:11:56,380 --> 00:12:00,380
In fact, I guess you could say that I'm a fan of anyone who considers themselves my fan.

237
00:12:00,380 --> 00:12:02,380
A fan of your fans?

238
00:12:03,380 --> 00:12:06,380
I'm never in the front, but they've found me in the shadows.

239
00:12:07,380 --> 00:12:12,380
They generously give me their love without condition, and I give them my love in return.

240
00:12:13,380 --> 00:12:17,380
Understand? I want them to know that if our roles reversed, I would be voting for them.

241
00:12:17,380 --> 00:12:18,380
Mwah!

242
00:12:18,380 --> 00:12:19,380
Oh!

243
00:12:19,380 --> 00:12:20,380
Mwah!

244
00:12:20,380 --> 00:12:21,380
Mwah!

245
00:12:21,380 --> 00:12:22,380
Mwah!

246
00:12:22,380 --> 00:12:23,380
Mwah!

247
00:12:23,380 --> 00:12:24,380
Mwah!

248
00:12:24,380 --> 00:12:25,380
Mwah!

249
00:12:25,380 --> 00:12:26,380
Mwah!

250
00:12:26,380 --> 00:12:27,380
Good morning!

251
00:12:27,380 --> 00:12:28,380
What?

252
00:12:28,380 --> 00:12:30,380
Makoto, you're still wearing pajamas!

253
00:12:30,380 --> 00:12:40,260
Good morning!

254
00:12:41,180 --> 00:12:41,780
What?

255
00:12:42,560 --> 00:12:44,280
Makoto, you're still wearing pajamas.

256
00:12:44,960 --> 00:12:48,620
We have a nasty habit of practicing and working on the days we have off.

257
00:12:48,800 --> 00:12:50,960
But this time I'm going to sleep all day.

258
00:12:51,360 --> 00:12:53,540
Come on, Sandman, take me away.

259
00:12:54,200 --> 00:12:55,940
Yeah, I'm sleeping too.

260
00:12:55,940 --> 00:12:58,500
And like any good cat, I'm going to sleep on your face.

261
00:12:58,500 --> 00:13:01,020
It's the day before the general elections.

262
00:13:01,320 --> 00:13:03,480
Should we really be relaxing like this?

263
00:13:03,520 --> 00:13:05,620
It's not like we have any control over it.

264
00:13:05,760 --> 00:13:07,480
We weren't ranked during the preliminaries.

265
00:13:08,140 --> 00:13:08,360
Huh?

266
00:13:09,340 --> 00:13:10,400
Yeah, that's right.

267
00:13:10,520 --> 00:13:12,680
At first I was really scared of the general elections,

268
